    "Requirement Analysis": "Functional scope: A headless Video Downloader core with URL validation, format selection, queue lifecycle, progress and cancellation, safe output naming, and an offline deterministic transfer adapter for tests. Protocol preservation: Strict Java protocol with pom.xml, Main.java, and MainTest.java; Maven Surefire and JUnit Jupiter for tests. Testability: Deterministic adapter ensures stable progress; tests avoid network and filesystem writes; runtime demo is non-interactive.\n\nArchitecture overview:\n- Canonical public API: VideoDownloader orchestrates a queue of DownloadTask using a TransferAdapter. Validation and naming utilities are pure functions. Formats and statuses are enums. OfflineDeterministicAdapter implements TransferAdapter and produces deterministic sessions.\n- Separation of concerns: Domain (requests, tasks, queue, sanitization) is separated from transfer boundary. No filesystem writes or real network.\n\nFull API spec (all public types/functions, exact signatures and behavior):\n- class DownloadFormat\n  - public static DownloadFormat fromExtension(String ext): Returns a supported format for a given extension (case-insensitive). Throws IllegalArgumentException for unsupported ext or null.\n  - public String defaultExtension(): Returns canonical lowercase extension for the format (e.g., \"mp4\").\n  - Supported enum constants: MP4, MP3, WEBM.\n- class ValidationUtils\n  - public static boolean isValidUrl(String url): Returns true for http/https URLs with host and optional path; rejects null/empty, spaces, invalid schemes, missing host.\n  - public static String sanitizeName(String name): Returns a safe base name by stripping unsafe characters, trimming, replacing spaces with underscores, and ensuring non-empty (falls back to \"download\").\n  - public static String withExtension(String baseName, DownloadFormat format): Returns baseName + \".\" + format.defaultExtension(); baseName sanitized; throws IllegalArgumentException if format is null.\n- class VideoDownloadRequest\n  - public static VideoDownloadRequest of(String url, DownloadFormat format, String suggestedName): Validates url/format; computes outputName via ValidationUtils; throws IllegalArgumentException on invalid input.\n  - public String getUrl(): Returns original URL.\n  - public DownloadFormat getFormat(): Returns format.\n  - public String getSuggestedName(): Returns original suggested name.\n  - public String getOutputName(): Returns sanitized name with extension; non-null.\n- enum DownloadStatus: PENDING, RUNNING, COMPLETED, FAILED, CANCELLED.\n- interface TransferAdapter\n  - public TransferSession begin(String url, DownloadFormat format, String outputName, ProgressListener listener): Starts a session; must be non-blocking; returns a session tracking total/downloaded bytes. Throws IllegalArgumentException on invalid arguments.\n- interface TransferSession\n  - public boolean step(): Advances transfer by one deterministic chunk; returns false when finished or cancelled; never blocks.\n  - public void cancel(): Idempotent; stops future progress.\n  - public long getTotalBytes(): Deterministic total bytes for this session.\n  - public long getDownloadedBytes(): Bytes transferred so far.\n- interface ProgressListener\n  - public void onProgress(long downloaded, long total): Called after each step; must be lightweight and exception-free.\n  - public void onCompleted(): Called exactly once when transfer reaches total.\n  - public void onFailed(String message): Called on failure, with message; not used by offline adapter.\n- class OfflineDeterministicAdapter implements TransferAdapter\n  - public TransferSession begin(...): Produces deterministic total size based on URL string hash and fixed chunk size; steps accumulate until completed; calls listener callbacks.\n- class DownloadTask\n  - public DownloadTask(int id, VideoDownloadRequest request): Constructs a task with PENDING status.\n  - public int getId(): Returns task identifier.\n  - public DownloadStatus getStatus(): Returns current status.\n  - public int getProgress(): Returns percentage 0..100 based on session bytes; 0 for PENDING; 100 for COMPLETED.\n  - public String getOutputName(): Returns request.getOutputName().\n  - public void start(TransferAdapter adapter): Transitions to RUNNING and attaches a session with listener updates.\n  - public void tick(): If RUNNING, calls session.step() and updates status when completed.\n  - public void cancel(): Cancels session if RUNNING and sets status to CANCELLED.\n- class VideoDownloader (canonical API)\n  - public VideoDownloader(TransferAdapter adapter): Requires non-null adapter.\n  - public int requestDownload(String url, DownloadFormat format, String suggestedName): Validates and enqueues; returns unique taskId; throws IllegalArgumentException on invalid input.\n  - public void startPending(): Starts all PENDING tasks; safe to call multiple times.\n  - public void tick(): Advances all RUNNING tasks by one step; non-blocking.\n  - public void cancel(int taskId): Cancels a task if RUNNING or PENDING; PENDING moves to CANCELLED without starting.\n  - public DownloadStatus getStatus(int taskId): Returns status or throws IllegalArgumentException if not found.\n  - public int getProgress(int taskId): Returns progress percentage or 0 for PENDING; throws IllegalArgumentException if not found.\n  - public String getOutputName(int taskId): Returns output name for the task or throws IllegalArgumentException if not found.\n\nPlanned files (exact list):\n- pom.xml\n- src/main/java/Main.java\n- src/main/java/DownloadFormat.java\n- src/main/java/ValidationUtils.java\n- src/main/java/VideoDownloadRequest.java\n- src/main/java/DownloadStatus.java\n- src/main/java/ProgressListener.java\n- src/main/java/TransferAdapter.java\n- src/main/java/TransferSession.java\n- src/main/java/OfflineDeterministicAdapter.java\n- src/main/java/DownloadTask.java\n- src/main/java/VideoDownloader.java\n- src/test/java/MainTest.java\n\nAllowed import direction (no cycles):\nValidationUtils, DownloadFormat, DownloadStatus -> used by VideoDownloadRequest.\nProgressListener, TransferAdapter, TransferSession -> implemented by OfflineDeterministicAdapter.\nVideoDownloadRequest, DownloadStatus, TransferSession -> used by DownloadTask.\nDownloadTask, TransferAdapter -> used by VideoDownloader.\nVideoDownloader, OfflineDeterministicAdapter -> used by Main and MainTest.\n\nEngineer code_todos (dependency-first ordered tasks with roles):\n1) pom.xml [Bob]\n- Declare Java 11 compiler settings.\n- Add junit-jupiter-api and junit-jupiter-engine (org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter) with test scope.\n- Configure maven-surefire-plugin to run JUnit 5.\n- Ensure default encoding and no preview features.\n\n2) DownloadFormat.java [Eve]\n- Implement enum for MP4, MP3, WEBM.\n- Provide fromExtension(String) and defaultExtension() as per API spec.\n- Validate input and throw IllegalArgumentException on unsupported values.\n\n3) ValidationUtils.java [Eve]\n- Implement isValidUrl(String) using URI parsing and scheme/host checks without network.\n- Implement sanitizeName(String) stripping unsafe characters, collapsing spaces to underscores, and fallback default.\n- Implement withExtension(String, DownloadFormat) combining sanitized name and canonical extension.\n\n4) DownloadStatus.java [Bob]\n- Implement enum: PENDING, RUNNING, COMPLETED, FAILED, CANCELLED.\n\n5) ProgressListener.java [Alex]\n- Define interface with onProgress, onCompleted, onFailed methods.\n\n6) TransferAdapter.java [Alex]\n- Define interface begin(String, DownloadFormat, String, ProgressListener) with argument validation expectations in doc comments.\n\n7) TransferSession.java [Alex]\n- Define interface step(), cancel(), getTotalBytes(), getDownloadedBytes() per API spec.\n\n8) VideoDownloadRequest.java [Eve]\n- Implement factory method of(url, format, name) validating via ValidationUtils and DownloadFormat.\n- Store fields and compute outputName.\n- Implement getters.\n\n9) OfflineDeterministicAdapter.java [Bob]\n- Implement TransferAdapter with nested OfflineDeterministicSession implementing TransferSession.\n- Use deterministic total bytes from stable hash of URL: for example, compute SHA-1-like simple hash and map to range [50_000, 200_000].\n- Use fixed chunk size (e.g., 4096 bytes) for step().\n- Call ProgressListener appropriately, ensure no blocking and idempotent cancel.\n\n10) DownloadTask.java [Eve]\n- Implement task state, attaching session in start(TransferAdapter) with listener updating internal progress.\n- Implement tick() to call session.step() and set COMPLETED when downloaded == total.\n- Implement cancel() handling RUNNING and PENDING statuses.\n- Expose getters id, status, progress, outputName.\n\n11) VideoDownloader.java [Alex]\n- Maintain Map<Integer, DownloadTask> and monotonically increasing id counter.\n- Implement requestDownload() to create VideoDownloadRequest and task; return id.\n- Implement startPending() to start all PENDING tasks using the adapter.\n- Implement tick() to advance RUNNING tasks.\n- Implement cancel(int) and getters for status/progress/outputName; validate task existence.\n\n12) Main.java [Bob]\n- Demonstrate: create OfflineDeterministicAdapter and VideoDownloader, enqueue two downloads, startPending, perform a few ticks, print statuses and progress, then exit.\n- No loops beyond a small fixed number of ticks; handle exceptions.\n\n13) src/test/java/MainTest.java [Alex]\n- JUnit Jupiter tests only.\n- Tests:\n  - testRuntimeWiringAndProgress: enqueue two downloads, startPending, tick until both complete with max iteration guard; assert COMPLETED and progress==100.\n  - testUrlValidationAndNaming: assert that invalid URL causes IllegalArgumentException; assert sanitize+extension behavior for suggested name.\n  - testCancellation: enqueue one, start, tick a few times, cancel and assert CANCELLED; further ticks keep progress unchanged.\n- Avoid inspecting private internals; use canonical public API.\n\nTesting plan:\n- All tests use OfflineDeterministicAdapter and VideoDownloader from canonical API.\n- No network, no filesystem, deterministic sizes/chunks.\n- Under 150 LOC, 3 tests covering wiring, validation/naming, cancellation.\n\nBuild and runtime:\n- pom.xml repeats the dependency contract: org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter (test scope) and Maven Surefire plugin that runs JUnit 5.\n- Main.java is default package and non-interactive; prints a brief demonstration and exits.\n\nSize control:\n- Each file under 150 LOC; no file exceeds 220 LOC.\n- Approximately 12 repository files including build and test; ~30 methods total.",
