    "Full API spec": "pom.xml: Maven descriptor declaring Java 11 compiler plugin, junit-jupiter dependency with test scope, and maven-surefire-plugin (version 3.1.2 or compatible) to run JUnit 5 tests. The single test file is src/test/java/MainTest.java, test command 'mvn -q test'.\n\nsrc/main/java/DownloadFormat.java: public enum DownloadFormat { MP4, WEBM; public static DownloadFormat fromExtension(String ext); public String defaultExtension(); } Semantics: fromExtension maps 'mp4' and 'webm' (case-insensitive) to respective enum constants; throws IllegalArgumentException for unknown or null/empty ext. defaultExtension returns '.mp4' for MP4 and '.webm' for WEBM.\n\nsrc/main/java/ValidationUtils.java: public final class ValidationUtils { public static boolean isValidUrl(String url); public static String sanitizeName(String name); public static String withExtension(String baseName, DownloadFormat format); } Semantics: isValidUrl returns true only for non-null URLs with scheme http or https, at least one '.', and no spaces; does not perform network I/O. sanitizeName trims, replaces any sequence of non-alphanumeric ('a'-'z','A'-'Z','0'-'9'), dash, underscore, or dot with a single underscore, collapses spaces to underscores, and ensures non-empty result (returns 'download' if sanitized becomes empty). withExtension appends format.defaultExtension() to sanitized baseName, ensuring baseName does not already end with that extension; throws IllegalArgumentException if format is null.\n\nsrc/main/java/VideoDownloadRequest.java: public final class VideoDownloadRequest { private final String url; private final DownloadFormat format; private final String suggestedName; private final String outputName; public static VideoDownloadRequest of(String url, DownloadFormat format, String suggestedName); public String getUrl(); public DownloadFormat getFormat(); public String getSuggestedName(); public String getOutputName(); } Semantics: of validates inputs: url must pass ValidationUtils.isValidUrl; format and suggestedName must be non-null; outputName computed as ValidationUtils.withExtension(ValidationUtils.sanitizeName(suggestedName), format). Throws IllegalArgumentException on invalid inputs. All getters return construction-time values.\n\nsrc/main/java/DownloadStatus.java: public enum DownloadStatus { PENDING, RUNNING, COMPLETED, FAILED, CANCELLED; } Semantics: State machine statuses; transitions governed by DownloadTask as described below.\n\nsrc/main/java/ProgressListener.java: public interface ProgressListener { void onProgress(long downloaded, long total); void onCompleted(); void onFailed(String message); } Semantics: callback boundaries; implementations must be non-blocking and avoid throwing exceptions.\n\nsrc/main/java/TransferSession.java: public interface TransferSession { boolean step(); void cancel(); long getTotalBytes(); long getDownloadedBytes(); } Semantics: step advances exactly one deterministic transfer chunk, returns true if more steps remain after the step; returns false when no more steps; cancel stops the session and leaves it in a terminal state with downloaded <= total; total and downloaded are non-negative.\n\nsrc/main/java/TransferAdapter.java: public interface TransferAdapter { TransferSession begin(String url, DownloadFormat format, String outputName, ProgressListener listener); } Semantics: begin starts a new deterministic session. May throw IllegalArgumentException on invalid arguments; must not perform network I/O in this project.\n\nsrc/main/java/OfflineDeterministicAdapter.java: public final class OfflineDeterministicAdapter implements TransferAdapter { public TransferSession begin(String url, DownloadFormat format, String outputName, ProgressListener listener); } Semantics: begin validates non-null args and returns a deterministic TransferSession with: totalBytes = 1000; per-step increments of 100 until reaching totalBytes; on each step it invokes listener.onProgress(downloaded, total); when downloaded == total it invokes listener.onCompleted(); cancel() stops further step(); step() after completion returns false always; step() after cancel returns false; listener.onFailed is not used in this deterministic implementation. Guarantees headless, offline operation.\n\nsrc/main/java/DownloadTask.java: public final class DownloadTask { private final int id; private final VideoDownloadRequest request; private DownloadStatus status; private TransferSession session; private int progress; public DownloadTask(int id, VideoDownloadRequest request); public int getId(); public DownloadStatus getStatus(); public int getProgress(); public String getOutputName(); public void start(TransferAdapter adapter); public void tick(); public void cancel(); } Semantics: Constructor initializes status = PENDING, progress = 0. start(adapter) requires current status == PENDING; creates a ProgressListener that updates 'progress' as (int) Math.round(100.0 * downloaded / total) clamped 0..100, sets status to RUNNING, and wires session via adapter.begin(). tick(): if status == RUNNING and session != null, calls session.step(); recomputes progress; if session reports no more steps and progress == 100, sets status = COMPLETED; tick() when CANCELLED or COMPLETED or FAILED is a no-op. cancel(): if status is RUNNING or PENDING, cancels session (if non-null) and sets status to CANCELLED; idempotent if already terminal. Error behavior: IllegalStateException if start() called when not PENDING.\n\nsrc/main/java/VideoDownloader.java: public final class VideoDownloader { private final TransferAdapter adapter; private final java.util.Map<Integer, DownloadTask> tasks; private int nextId; public VideoDownloader(TransferAdapter adapter); public int requestDownload(String url, DownloadFormat format, String suggestedName); public void startPending(); public void tick(); public void cancel(int taskId); public DownloadStatus getStatus(int taskId); public int getProgress(int taskId); public String getOutputName(int taskId); } Semantics: Constructor requires non-null adapter. requestDownload creates VideoDownloadRequest.of and a new DownloadTask with id = nextId++, stores it, returns id. startPending starts all tasks with status PENDING. tick advances all RUNNING tasks by calling DownloadTask.tick(). cancel looks up task by id and calls task.cancel(); throws IllegalArgumentException if id unknown. getStatus/getProgress/getOutputName return properties for existing tasks; each throws IllegalArgumentException if id unknown.\n\nsrc/main/java/Main.java: public final class Main { public static void main(String[] args); } Semantics: Demonstrates wiring by creating OfflineDeterministicAdapter and VideoDownloader, enqueuing two downloads, starting pending, ticking a few iterations, and printing status/progress; exits deterministically without long-running loops.\n\nsrc/test/java/MainTest.java: JUnit 5 tests using org.junit.jupiter.api.*. Tests import VideoDownloader, OfflineDeterministicAdapter, DownloadFormat, DownloadStatus. Tests must not touch environment-dependent behavior beyond OfflineDeterministicAdapter; no network or file system access.\n\nAllowed import direction: Core domain modules (DownloadFormat, ValidationUtils, VideoDownloadRequest, DownloadStatus, ProgressListener, TransferAdapter, TransferSession, DownloadTask, VideoDownloader) must not import Main or OfflineDeterministicAdapter. OfflineDeterministicAdapter may import core interfaces only. Main imports the canonical public API (VideoDownloader, OfflineDeterministicAdapter, DownloadFormat). Tests import only canonical public API classes from src/main/java. Callers/tests must not invent aliases or alternate signatures.",
    "Shared Knowledge": "The build uses Maven with Java 11 and JUnit Jupiter via Surefire. All classes live in the default package under src/main/java to avoid package mismatch. The canonical public API consists of VideoDownloader (orchestration), DownloadTask (single-task state machine), VideoDownloadRequest (value object), DownloadFormat, ValidationUtils, DownloadStatus, ProgressListener, TransferAdapter, and TransferSession. OfflineDeterministicAdapter is the deterministic environment boundary used by Main and tests. The single test file src/test/java/MainTest.java imports only VideoDownloader, OfflineDeterministicAdapter, DownloadFormat, and DownloadStatus, and asserts deterministic progress/completion, naming/validation rules, and cancellation. Main provides a thin runtime demo and does not affect tests.",
    "Execution Protocol": "Test command: 'mvn -q test'. Runtime entry: src/main/java/Main.java. Single protocol test target: src/test/java/MainTest.java. Tests are headless, offline, and deterministic; they require no manual interaction. Exactly one protocol-level test file is present. Additional implementation files do not alter protocol files.",
